From 003ecc0adcb8d2d84b607a856e7a55a457b183a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:20:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] S2-9: the workshop's weapon picture composed in slices
 (weld_slice.c)

weld_view_image_sliced() / weld_view_prefetch(): the 96x64 first-person
picture of Rivet's workshop is composed over a few ticks (GBA: in the
frames' idle time; PS1: inside the frame while the platform has room)
while the picture shown before stays up, and the pictures that come next
are composed ahead. weld_slice.c builds weld_gfx.c's recipes a second
time on primitives that can stop and go on, with faster rows (the same
pixels: test_weld_slice compares both builds over thousands of weapons).
Other platforms compose in the call as before (weld_view_image).

GBA: two more pictures live in the portrait cache's block pool
(portrait_pool_big). cross-stream: portrait.c / portrait.h get that one
entry point (not built on the PS1); nothing else of the portrait cache
changes. The PS1 keeps the job's state in the overlay slot's scene
scratch: no new resident byte.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
